# /etc/fstab -- the filesystems of a LikeOS installation
#
# This is the template in the system image (likeos-rootfs.tar.zst).  The
# installer writes the real file when it installs LikeOS: a line for the
# root and one for the EFI system partition, both by filesystem UUID,
#
#   UUID=<root uuid>  /          ext4  defaults                    0  1
#   UUID=<esp uuid>   /boot/efi  vfat  umask=0077,shortname=mixed  0  2
#
# and below them every line of this file that is not a comment and does not
# mount / or /boot/efi.  A line added here for all installations is kept.
#
# Format, one filesystem per line (see fstab(5)):
#
#   <file system>  <mount point>  <type>  <options>  <dump>  <pass>
#
# init mounts every line but the root (which the kernel mounts) at
# start-up, checking the filesystems with a pass number above 0 first
# (pass 1 before pass 2).  Devices are best named by UUID=, LABEL=,
# PARTUUID= or PARTLABEL=, which stay the same when disks are added.
#
